--- !u!114 &546955058
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 546955056}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
    m_TypeName: UnityEngine.UI.MaskableGraphic+CullStateChangedEvent, UnityEngine.UI,
      Version=1.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null
  m_text: "Abakhanskya, often referred to as the Matron, is a woman who has been around
    for a long, long\r\ntime. The uninitiated may see her as a wandering giant, a
    dragon on two legs who carries out the\r\nsame task. But she differs. Whilst a
    dragon has its minions, it carries little in terms of end goal,\r\nbeyond amassing
    wealth. And a giant typically lacks a vision for their future. Abakhanskya builds\r\ntowards
    a future in which she, and those who follow and worship her, rule with no interference.\r\n\r\nTypically
    isolationist, whenever she has appeared, it has been because of outside forces
    bringing her\r\nattention to the outside world. It is hard to obtain access to
    her dwellings and communities without\r\nbecoming fuel for either her or a worshipper.\r\n\r\nIt
    is unknown how long she has been existing for. It is typically said in several
    local stories she's\r\nbeen around for a thousand years. She herself, even occasionally
    has admitted to once being human.\r\nHer closest entourage are those akin to her,
    yet far smaller. They are referred to as 'Kasimirans', and\r\nshe is one of them,
    their Matron \u2013 in fact, she says she is the Matron of all, who but submit
    and play\r\ntheir role to her.\r\n\r\nWhen brought forth onto the world stage,
    she is a force no one wants to face on their own. Her\r\npracticed expertise has
    made itself known again and again. It is said that generations of peoples are\r\nwhat
    line her form, of any race and walk of life. Her voracity does not discriminate
    and her skills\r\nand knowledge do not fail her.\r\n\r\nStanding at nearly six
    metres tall, she's thrice as tall as the typical two-legged and towers over even\r\ndragons.
    She has an armoured hide all over, even more so in areas beyond her underbelly.
    Arrows\r\nhave been said to plink off her hide harmlessly and even wall targeted
    blows barely cause her\r\nannoyance. Warriors throughout history have said, 'Go
    for the eyes!'\r\n\r\nAs to her origin, it is unsure. But her open admission to
    being human at one point is a clue. Some\r\nsay she has from an Earth in a time
    unlike another. Some say she drank the blood of a dragon she\r\nconquered in battle,
    then betrayed her comrades. And some say it is but a trick to fool mortal races\r\ninto
    believing she too is mortal, for they know she loves playing with her foes.\r\n\r\nNevertheless,
    she carries an extreme knowledge and expertise. May hope be given to her foes,
    for\r\nthere is little else to console them."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
