      Version=1.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null
  m_text: "About the Skysharks\r\nThe Skysharks, Sky Sharks or Sharks, all forms used
    locally both officially and unofficially, are creatures very much reminiscent
    of the great white shark of Earth, with the very notable exception that aside
    from swimming in the water, they can also \"swim\" in the air.\r\n\nAveraging
    close to twenty feet in length, the Skysharks are larger than great white's  on
    Earth, but have mostly the same properties otherwise. Often seen in the company
    of the Dark Swallowers, another being resembling flying Earth fish, the Skysharks
    travel in small packs, preying on other monsters, travellers, armies and entire
    towns, both able and eager to fill their stretchy bellies with anything living.
    \r\n\nThe method they use to fly is unknown, but allows them to reach speeds of
    up to 50mph in air, likely due to lower resistance compared to water. Despite
    the strength of their ability to fly, Skysharks have been known to ground themselves
    with overt gluttony, leaving them to drag their bellies along the ground until
    they have digested enough of their prey to regain flight.\r\n\nWhile not a significant
    difference, since the Skysharks are among the less sexually active creatures in
    this world, the males can be told apart from the females by the presence of their
    claspers, just as with Earth sharks.\r\n\nClassification according to local system:
    Large monster, Fish like, Skyshark\r\nSize: Large\r\nStrength: High\r\nDodge:
    Below Average\r\nHealth: High\r\nVoracity: High"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
