    m_TypeName: UnityEngine.UI.MaskableGraphic+CullStateChangedEvent, UnityEngine.UI,
      Version=1.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null
  m_text: "About: The Harvesters\r\n The appearance of the Harvesters is best explained
    by thinking of a snake. A snake with a rigid bony shell covering its head, two
    scythe blades on short jointed limbs growing from little below the head, about
    a third of their length held straight up from the ground, rising to a height of
    seven to nine feet.\r\n Their names derive partly from their scythes, which they
    use to cut down their foes, but also from the way they gather their food, harvesting
    entire villages and towns for their food, and possibly for slaves. Harvesters
    are deservedly among the more feared of this worlds predators, especially since
    they do not seem to be mere animals.\r\n While no-one is known to have ever held
    an actual conversation with a Harvester, they have been seen congregating in what
    appears to be a discussion, with the Harvesters motioning to each other and pointing
    out things around them, apparently planning their actions. Yet no sound has ever
    been reported to have been heard, all Harvesters remaining eerily silent at all
    times. Whether this indicates a method of communication not relying on sound,
    or merely sounds inaudible to all civilized races of this world, isn't known.\r\n
    The least well understood part of the Harvesters is their origin. Despite a firm
    presence on this world, they do not seem to either dwell or breed here. While
    it is fairly normal for new creatures to appear from portals now and then, the
    Harvesters seem able to create similar portals intentionally, not only arriving
    by them but sometimes leaving as well, taking their harvest with them.\r\n The
    Harvesters method of feeding is the least unusual of their traits. They catch
    a hold of their prey with their mouths and lift them up to toss them down their
    gullets, occasionally aiding the process by manouvering their food with their
    scythe limbs.\r\n The organ the harvesters have just above the point where their
    upward portion meets the ground looks much like a thick, partially prehensile
    penis, able to slide forth from a slit in the creatures skin, but cutting open
    dead Harvesters has shown that the organ is more of an ovipositor. Feeding seems
    to excite the Harvesters sufficiently for the organ to emerge in readiness, a
    connection that some have taken as an indication of the possible fate of those
    harvested who aren't digested.\r\nClassification according to local system: Advanced
    monster, Alien, Harvester\r\nSize: Largeish\r\nStrength: High\r\nDodge: Good\r\nHealth:
    High\r\nVoracity: Very High\r\nSpecial note: Avoid at all cost.\r\n\r\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
