  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
    m_TypeName: UnityEngine.UI.MaskableGraphic+CullStateChangedEvent, UnityEngine.UI,
      Version=1.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null
  m_text: "About the Compy\r\nResembling the fossils of dinosaurs, but significantly
    smaller than any found on Earth, these small creatures resembling lizards walking
    on two feet are called Compy by the locals.\r\n\nAveraging two feet from snout
    to tip of the tail, their heads raising barely above my knee at highest, the Compy
    are considered among the least dangerous of the local predators. Indeed, they
    are often kept as pets, or even as a kind of cattle for consumption. They occasionally
    cause havoc in villages and towns when going wild, their natural curiosity and
    tendency to get everywhere causing property damage and rarely casualties. They
    are also common sight in the wild, often attacking prey far larger than anything
    they have any hope of bringing down, or keeping down.\r\n\nBeing reptilian, or
    reptilian like, they have no external genitalia when not in state of arousal.
    When exited, their cloaca stretches open to allow for approximately five inch
    long, tapering penis to slide out, curving under their bellies. One might wonder
    what use this organ has, since no-one can say they have ever seen a female Compy.
    The entire species seems to be male, and indeed, they never breed in captivity,
    though not for a lack of trying. In the wild a steady supply of them keeps appearing
    though, suggesting the females might be rare, yet spawning massive amounts of
    males to roam the land. How such is a viable or sensible survival strategy for
    the species eludes me, and the locals simply shrug at it, regularly seeing things
    even more bizarre.\r\n\nUnusually for the predators of this world, the Compy cannot
    stretch their jaws around anything larger than what a person from Earth might
    expect. Indeed, they rarely even eat anything solid. Instead, the hunting method
    of the Compy seems to be to engulf their prey with their penises, the members
    seemingly capable of stretching around objects as large as an adult cow. The prey
    are then pulled further in, deposited inside their testicles, which stretch from
    not even being visible when the Compy are unaroused, to being a slight bump when
    aroused, to even containing multiple humans within their circumferance.\r\n\nThe
    prey are then \"digested\" into what seems similar to the creatures normal seed,
    and is used much like milk by some communities. Left to their own, the creatures
    feed this thick white soup to each other, or curl to drink their own produce,
    explaining their lack of need for expanding jaws. Their bellies can seemingly
    stretch like those of other local beings though, their feedings sometimes leaving
    them as protrusions from the side of their own large, round, sloshing guts.\r\n\nClassification
    according to local system: Small monster, Lizard, Compy\r\nSize: Minimal\r\nStrength:
    Very Low\r\nDodge: Very Good\r\nHealth: Poor\r\nVoracity: High"
